{"_format": "See js/city.js, js/outskirts.js (the river, bridges, boats, business zones, hand-placed towers), js/downtown.js (skybridges), js/metro.js (line A, the train hoops) and js/skylight.js (the night preset: the moon is the sun). Downtown is at (0, 0). The route runs west up the river from the east, between riverside towers: between the piers of two low bridges (a 1 m corridor at those hoops keeps the piers), across the river and back, past a ship, under the suspension bridge; up onto line A's quay viaduct, where a train stands at the station: it pulls out as you pass the hoop before its own (wait, so its hoop never changes trains): a chase of a few seconds; round a wide bend into the avenue (x 660), where the hoop at its foot lets the next train go from the station further up: catch it up the tower canyon; under the skybridge between two towers across the avenue; west into the slalom round three towers, a hoop between each pair; under the second skybridge, a tight gap between two towers; through the needle, a gap between two towers, and round onto a long straight east to the tallest tower: pull up and climb its west face at the stick's steepest (on the jets' climb assist), over the top, the last hoop over its helipad (pad: no spire on it here); the climb is one set (js/aerobatic.js): miss a hoop or crash and it's all again from the pull-up. Laid out by work/design.py.", "id": "downtown", "name": "Downtown Run", "lead": "Up the river and into the towers at night.", "seeds": {"a": 61, "b": 29, "c": 47, "trees": 13}, "terrain": {"size": 8400, "cx": 1500, "cz": 300, "n": 440, "water": 12, "edge": 20, "carveR": 300, "micro": 0}, "relief": {"base": 26, "amp": 220, "pow": 2.4, "freq": 0.0009, "ridgeAmp": 30, "ridgeFreq": 0.002}, "palette": {"dry": [60, 200], "forestTop": [160, 260], "high": [240, 330], "pathTint": false}, "lake": null, "hills": [], "trees": {"near": 0, "scattered": 2500, "minAlt": 24, "maxAlt": 260, "mask": 0.5}, "view": {"near": 1, "far": 9000, "f